<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 4 September, from 476 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,550 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Odoacer deposes Romulus Augustulus, the last Western emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Germanic commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed the boy emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> and sent the imperial regalia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. The date is conventionally taken as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/626">626 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,400 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Li Shimin takes the Tang throne as Emperor Taizong</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a>, who had encouraged his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-gaozu-of-tang">Li Yuan</a>'s rebellion against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a>, took the throne as the second Tang emperor, known after his death as Taizong. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-turkic-khaganate">Eastern Turkic Khaganate</a> and extended Tang power into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Emperor Taizong of Tang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/929">929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,097 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Saxon army destroys a Slavic army at Lenzen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the Linones stronghold of Lenzen, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> army of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> Bernhard destroyed an army of the Slavic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redarii">Redarii</a>. The battle marked the failure of Slavic resistance to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a>'s expansion to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redarii">Redarii</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1260">1260 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">766 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Siena's Ghibellines rout the Florentine Guelphs at Montaperti</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Siena, Sienese Ghibellines, Florentine exiles under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farinata-degli-uberti">Farinata degli Uberti</a> and German cavalry sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manfred-king-of-sicily">Manfred of Sicily</a> routed the Guelph army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>. The Ghibellines then held Florence until after the Angevin victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a> in 1266.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-montaperti">Battle of Montaperti</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guelphs-and-ghibellines">Guelphs and Ghibellines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1479">1479 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">547 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Castile and Portugal make peace in the Treaty of Alcáçovas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Catholic Monarchs and Afonso V of Portugal and his son, Prince John, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-castilian-succession">War of the Castilian Succession</a>. Afonso recognised Isabella I as queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, which kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canary-islands">Canary Islands</a>, while Portugal gained hegemony in the Atlantic.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-alcacovas">Treaty of Alcáçovas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-portugal">John II of Portugal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1781">1781 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spanish settlers found the pueblo of Los Angeles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forty-four settlers of mixed Spanish, Native and African ancestry founded a farming town near the Porciúncula River. El Pueblo de la Reina de los Ángeles grew into the second-largest US city.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1888">1888 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">138 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Eastman patents the Kodak roll-film camera</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Eastman received a patent for his Kodak box camera. Sold pre-loaded with film under the slogan 'You press the button, we do the rest', it made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/photography">photography</a> a mass pastime.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1957">1957 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">69 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arkansas National Guard blocks Black students at Little Rock</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor Orval Faubus used the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-panama">National Guard</a> to stop nine Black students entering Little Rock Central High School. Later in the month <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> sent federal troops to enforce desegregation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Larry Page and Sergey Brin incorporate Google</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Stanford PhD students incorporated Google, working from a rented garage in Menlo Park. Its search engine became the gateway to the web and the company one of the world's most valuable.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 4 September <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alexander-iii-of-scotland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alexander-iii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Alexander III of Scotland</span><span class="tp">1241–1286</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-viii-duke-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-viii-duke-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amadeus VIII, Duke of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1383–1451</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wanli-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wanli-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wanli Emperor</span><span class="tp">1563–1620</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dadabhai-naoroji"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dadabhai-naoroji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dadabhai Naoroji</span><span class="tp">1825–1917</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luigi-cadorna"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luigi-cadorna.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luigi Cadorna</span><span class="tp">1850–1928</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/karlis-ulmanis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/karlis-ulmanis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Kārlis Ulmanis</span><span class="tp">1877–1942</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 4 September <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bermudo-iii-of-leon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bermudo-iii-of-leon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bermudo III of León</span><span class="tp">c. 1017–1037</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-dudley-1st-earl-of-leicester"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-dudley-1st-earl-of-leicester.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Dudley, 1st Earl of Leicester</span><span class="tp">c. 1532–1588</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-miguel-carrera"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-miguel-carrera.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José Miguel Carrera</span><span class="tp">1785–1821</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edvard-grieg"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Edvard Grieg</span><span class="tp">1843–1907</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-schuman"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-schuman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Schuman</span><span class="tp">1886–1963</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-schweitzer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-schweitzer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Schweitzer</span><span class="tp">1875–1965</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
